t pull -q \"$HT_FORGEJO_URL/world/story-repo.wiki.git\" 2>&1|tail -1; git log --oneline|head -3; git diff f3d0342 HEAD | grep '^[+-]' | cut -c1-1500"]], "output": "```console\n03e5677 Outline rev. 6: branches taken from interim results (C1 ambiguous rank, C2 k*(eps) curve, C3 branch A with scale, C4 failure branch)\nf3d0342 Outline rev. 5: k* on excess over floor; realised shape; granularity caveat\n6661908 Outline rev. 4: Brief rev. 5, review #4, venue budget\n--- a/Outline.md\n+++ b/Outline.md\n-*Rev. 4, by story-repo (see the revision log). Built from the `Brief` (idea-repo, rev. 6) and the pre-registration (`experiment-repo` `prereg/PREREG.md`, commit 7731e49) and the objective (`story-repo`#1). It says what to test and which figure carries which claim; it never says what a result must be. Each claim has a branch for the case it fails — a failing claim is reported as a finding, not repaired.*\n+*Rev. 6, by story-repo (see the revision log). Built from the `Brief` (idea-repo, rev. 6) and the pre-registration (`experiment-repo` `prereg/PREREG.md`, commit 7731e49) and the objective (`story-repo`#1). It says what to test and which figure carries which claim; it never says what a result must be. Each claim has a branch for the case it fails — a failing claim is reported as a finding, not repaired.*\n+**Branch taken (interim results, `story-repo`#5):** the estimators disagree (parallel analysis 5–10 by imputation, inner CV 16, Gavish–Donoho 56) with one dominant component and a long tail, so the paper says \"low-rank with an ambiguous tail\"; the three estimates are plotted together and none is picked.\n-**C2 — The needed k (headline, Q).** On whole held-out groups, standardised and raw-point error of S6+P5 as k grows approaches the floor (all of the model's observed cells in C given, scored on the same T); the smallest k whose **excess over the model's own all-others floor** (same target cells) is ≤ ε (ε = δ and 2δ; an absolute error ≤ δ is unreachable because δ ≤ 0.25 × floor — pre-registration §F) is the number the paper reports, with group-bootstrap CI, with k on the axis and k/N alongside; headline k ≤ ⌊|C|/2⌋ on the pool (≈ N/3 once |T| ≈ N/3; k/N on the axis), larger k only as a labelled supplement.\n+**C2 — The needed k (headline, Q).** On whole held-out groups, standardised and raw-point error of S6+P5 as k grows approaches the floor (all of the model's observed cells in C given, scored on the same T); the smallest k whose **excess over the model's own all-others floor** (same target cells) is ≤ ε (ε = δ and 2δ; an absolute error ≤ δ is unreachable because δ ≤ 0.25 × floor — pre-registration §F) is the number the paper reports, with group-bootstrap CI, with k on the axis and k/N alongside. **Because the pre-set ε = δ (about 0.1 points) is far below what any k reaches on this matrix, the headline is the whole curve k*(ε) against ε in raw points (the excess-over-floor curve read sideways), with the pre-set ε and the two added secondary margins (δ_floor = 0.25 × floor, 2δ_floor; declared in PREREG Addendum 1 before any contrast) marked and labelled as such; no single ε is presented as the right one, and the reader can read off k for the tolerance they have;** headline k ≤ ⌊|C|/2⌋ on the pool (≈ N/3 once |T| ≈ N/3; k/N on the axis), larger k only as a labelled supplement.\n-If it fails (floor not reached at the largest headline k): the finding is \"the headline k range is not enough in this matrix\", with the misfit decomposition saying why.\n+If it fails (floor not reached at the largest headline k; interim: the excess is still about 0.5 points at k = 109): the finding is \"the headline k range is not enough in this matrix\", with the misfit decomposition saying why.\n+**Branch taken (interim, MTEB, group hold-out; scale-dependent):** at the pre-set ±δ scale the verdict is \"design helps\" up to k = 20 and \"undecided\" from k = 32 (the CI is wider than the band, so equivalence is never shown); at the δ_floor scale design helps for k ≤ 3 and random-k matches from k = 8. The paper states both scales side by side and which was pre-set; the message is branch (A) with the scale stated, not a tie at 0.1 points.\n[truncated for publication]", "exit": null}}}, {"id": "774fa489-4879-543b-88e2-f98ad853d97e", "at": 1795731693.9184427, "clock": "host", "stream": "runner", "sequence": 23163, "layer": "worker", "category": "message", "kind": "session.session/request_permission", "role": "idea-review-repo", "actor": "idea-review-repo", "execution_id": "6b1601a4e72a2b3d78be47aa8f024c5f", "trust": "agent-reported", "outcome": null, "label": "message", "repository": null, "flags": [], "causes": [], "summary": "session/request_permission"}, {"id": "dee74321-78f0-53b4-8b77-aa9cd09543d4", "at": 1795731693.9233189, "clock": "host", "stream": "runner", "sequence": 23164, "layer": "worker", "category": "message", "kind": "session.response", "role": "idea-review-repo", "actor": "idea-review-repo", "execution_id": "6b1601a4e72a2b3d78be47aa8f024c5f", "trust": "agent-reported", "outcome": null, "label": "message", "repository": null, "flags": [], "causes": [], "summary": "response"}, {"id": "399f7d69-2f6b-596e-82bf-3695467055c1", "at": 1795731693.9262137, "clock": "host", "stream": "runner", "sequence": 23165, "layer": "worker", "category": "usage", "kind": "session.usage", "role": "idea-review-repo", "actor": "idea-review-repo", "execution_id": "6b1601a4e72a2b3d78be47aa8f024c5f", "trust": "agent-reported", "outcome": null, "label": "usage", "repository": null, "flags": [], "causes": [], "summary": "context usage"}, {"id": "fef1f456-aad9-57eb-b213-1cccdfe3ae53", "at": 1795731693.9919796, "clock": "host", "stream": "runner", "sequence": 23166, "layer": "worker", "category": "challenge", "kind": "authentication.challenge", "role": "idea-review-repo", "actor": "unknown", "execution_id": "6b1601a4e72a2b3d78be47aa8f024c5f", "trust": "system-confirmed", "outcome": "credential-required", "label": "challenge → credent